{"type":"definition","type_name":"Definition","number":"4.5.5","title":"Contradictory, Contrary and Subcontrary Formulas","title_html":"Contradictory, Contrary and Subcontrary Formulas","html":"<p>Formulas <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D711 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>φ</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> and <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\psi\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D713 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ψ</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> are <strong>contradictory</strong>\nif every row makes exactly one of them true; <strong>contrary</strong>\nif no row makes both true but some row makes both false;\n<strong>subcontrary</strong> if no row makes both false but some row\nmakes both true.</p>","file":"ch4/entailment-and-equivalence.html"}